.TH COF-WIZARD 1 "2026-11-13" "cof 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cof-wizard \- Build an orchestration by talking to the wizard, headlessly;
unlike \fBcof gen\fR, it asks clarifying questions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
cof wizard [OPTIONS]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Builds an orchestration headlessly by talking to the bundled wizard
orchestration, from a one-line --goal, rather than a single prompt -- a
multi-turn, clarifying-questions build. Not cof gen, which drives a different,
single-shot orchestration.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --goal, -g
\fIGOAL\fR One-line description of what the orchestration should do.
.TP
.B --name, -n
\fINAME\fR Name for the result (used for the filename / library slug). Derived
from --goal if omitted.
.TP
.B --category
\fICATEGORY\fR One of: recipes, patterns, utilities, agents, learn. [default:
recipes]
.TP
.B --reply, -r
\fIREPLY\fR File of scripted replies, one per line, used instead of stdin.
.TP
.B --out, -o
\fIOUT\fR Write the final YAML here (default: stdout).
.TP
.B --library
Also save into the local library, indexed like a bundled entry.
.TP
.B --max-turns
\fIMAX_TURNS\fR Stop after this many turns. [default: 10]
.TP
.B --config, -c
\fICONFIG\fR Path to config JSON.
.TP
.B --verbose, -v
Show orchestration execution logs.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B cof wizard --goal 'summarize a URL and post it to slack'
Builds an orchestration through the wizard's questions.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_CONFIG
An explicit config JSON path (same as --config). When set, replaces the global
config and any project config entirely, rather than layering on top of them.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_MODEL
Overrides the resolved config's default_model.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_ADAPTER
Overrides the resolved config's default_adapter.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_ADAPTER_URL
Overrides the resolved default adapter's base_url.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_COMFYUI_URL
Overrides the comfyui plugin's base_url.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_SYSTEMONE_URL
Overrides the systemone plugin's base_url.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_ENABLED_ADAPTERS
Comma-separated allowlist, narrowing (never widening) the resolved config's
enabled_adapters.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_ENABLED_PLUGINS
Comma-separated allowlist, narrowing (never widening) the resolved config's
enabled_plugins.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_ENABLED_TOOLS
Comma-separated allowlist, narrowing (never widening) the resolved config's
enabled_tools.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_ENVIRONMENT
Overrides the resolved config's environment (dev, prod, or test).
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_TRUST_PROJECT_CONFIG
Trusts a project config in the current directory without running cof trust
first.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/circuitry/config.json
The global config, applied first; a trusted project config layers on top of
it.
.TP
.I ~/.config/circuitry/.env
Private environment variables, loaded before config resolution (written by cof
setup).
.TP
.I ~/.config/circuitry/trusted.json
Project configs trusted by cof trust; config resolution consults it before
applying a discovered project config.
.TP
.I ./circuitry.config.json, ./config.json
A project config in the working directory, layered on top of the global config
once trusted.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The command failed, or the input was invalid.
.TP
.B 2
A usage error -- an unrecognized option or missing argument.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBcof(1)\fR, \fBcof-gen(1)\fR, \fBcof-run(1)\fR
